{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the Sabbath-produce of the land, etc.</b> Even though I forbade them to you — I did not forbid them for eating or for benefit, but only that you must not treat them as the owner of the house; rather, everyone is equal in it — you, and your hired worker, and your resident." "<b>The Sabbath-produce of the land shall be yours for food.</b> You eat from what is abandoned, but you do not eat from what is guarded (Sifra)." "<b>For you, and for your slave, and for your maidservant.</b> Since it says ״וְאָכְלוּ אֶבְיֹנֵי עַמֶּךָ״ (Exodus 23), one might think they are forbidden for eating to the rich — Scripture says, ״לְךָ וּלְעַבְדְּךָ וְלַאֲמָתֶךָ״ — behold, owners and slaves and maidservants are stated here (Sifra)." "<b>And for your hired worker, and for your resident.</b> Even the gentiles (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:13.125847893Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}